  "implementation": [
    "Three additive pure APIs inspect approval-v3 header identity, retained dispatch assessment and retained dispatch position. Existing public entrypoints and result schemas remain unchanged.",
    "The v3 inspector binds exact actor/header, original canonical manifest text/hash, source codec, annual-binding envelope and predecessor identity. It does not fabricate XML/document values or establish source, review or annual-policy authority.",
    "Assessment and position validate full retained correspondence, then reuse ordered journal state and original payload/document/key identity. Confirmed, uncertain and blocked outcomes retain precedence; prepared without outcome remains uncertain.",
    "Any v3 approval or v2 source anywhere in typed input requires captured history, overrides and withdrawals, including a legacy target within mixed history. Both new readers require exact ActorId with USER and exact UserId. Legacy-only unknown coverage remains unknown.",
    "Small private extractions share header/predecessor and journal mechanics. Existing application, adapter, HTTP, SQL, recovery and correction callsites remain fixed; no fresh claim, intent or provider path is enabled."
  ],
